sequenceDiagram
    actor Mgr as Manager<br/>(Schedule.Create)
    participant Ctrl as ShiftMakerController
    participant Svc as ShiftScheduleService
    participant DB as Database

    Mgr->>Ctrl: Create schedule<br/>(name, work area, dates,<br/>rotation template or inline days)
    Ctrl->>Ctrl: Validate EndDate >= StartDate
    opt Custom rotation entered inline
        Ctrl->>DB: Create ad-hoc RotationTemplate<br/>"{ScheduleName} (auto)"
    end
    Ctrl->>Svc: CreateFromTemplateAsync(...)
    Svc->>DB: Insert ShiftSchedule (Status = Draft)
    Ctrl->>Svc: FillFromRotationAsync(scheduleId)
    Svc->>DB: Wipe + regenerate DailyGroupShift rows<br/>(5 groups x N days, using rotation<br/>template or DefaultRotation fallback)
    Ctrl->>Svc: GenerateAssignmentsAsync(scheduleId)
    Svc->>DB: Wipe + regenerate ShiftAssignment rows<br/>(one per active UserGroupMembership<br/>per plan slot)
    Svc-->>Ctrl: Done
    Ctrl-->>Mgr: Redirect to Details (calendar view)

    Mgr->>Ctrl: Publish
    Ctrl->>Svc: PublishScheduleAsync
    Svc->>DB: Status = Published
    Note over Mgr,DB: Non-scheduler employees can only<br/>see a schedule once Published.
